# Shared Avatar Generation Framework

Project-agnostic avatar/character image generation using the Leonardo.ai API.
Each project provides its own **JSON character definitions** while sharing the
generation engine, image post-processing pipeline, and selection GUI.

## Quick Start

```bash
# Install dependencies
pip install -r scripts/avatar-generation/requirements.txt

# Dry-run: validate prompts without API calls
python3 scripts/avatar-generation/generate.py \
    --characters toogether/characters/toogether-avatars.json \
    --dry-run --all

# Generate portraits for all characters (requires API key)
export LEONARDO_AI_API_KEY="your-key"
python3 scripts/avatar-generation/generate.py \
    --characters toogether/characters/toogether-avatars.json \
    --all --mode portrait --seed 42

# Generate org-spirits portraits
python3 scripts/avatar-generation/generate.py \
    --characters org-spirits-app/characters/org-spirits.json \
    --all --mode portrait

# Generate category key visuals
python3 scripts/avatar-generation/generate.py \
    --characters toogether/characters/category-visuals.json \
    --all --mode key_visual --seed 42

# Review and select avatars
pip install -r scripts/avatar-generation/selector/requirements.txt
python3 scripts/avatar-generation/selector/app.py \
    --characters toogether/characters/toogether-avatars.json \
    --avatars-dir toogether/generated-avatars
```

## Directory Structure

```
scripts/avatar-generation/
├── generate.py              ← Main CLI entry point
├── config.py                ← API defaults and configuration
├── leonardo_api.py          ← Leonardo.ai API client
├── image_processing.py      ← Pillow: circle crop, neon ring, composite
├── prompt_builder.py        ← Build prompts from JSON character definitions
├── requirements.txt         ← Python dependencies (requests, Pillow)
├── README.md                ← This file
├── characters/              ← Character definition files (JSON)
│   ├── schema.json          ← JSON Schema for validation
│   ├── toogether-avatars.json  ← 66 toogether characters
│   └── org-spirits.json     ← 5 org-spirits characters
└── selector/                ← Avatar selection GUI
    ├── app.py               ← Flask backend (loads from JSON)
    └── requirements.txt     ← Selector dependencies (Flask, Pillow, requests)
```

## Adding a New Project

1. **Create a character JSON file** in `characters/` following `schema.json`.
   Minimum required fields per character:
   - `name` — Display name
   - `character_prompt` — Character-specific prompt text

2. **Define project-wide style** in the `style` block:
   - `portrait_prompt` — Base style prepended to every portrait
   - `portrait_negative` — Negative prompt for portraits
   - `generation_params` — Leonardo.ai model, dimensions, steps

3. **Run a dry-run** to validate prompts:
   ```bash
   python3 scripts/avatar-generation/generate.py \
       --characters characters/my-project.json \
       --dry-run --all
   ```

4. **Generate images:**
   ```bash
   python3 scripts/avatar-generation/generate.py \
       --characters characters/my-project.json \
       --all --mode composite --seed 42 \
       --output my-project/generated-avatars
   ```

## CLI Reference

```
python3 scripts/avatar-generation/generate.py --characters <path> [options]

Required:
  --characters PATH    Path to JSON character definition file

Selection (mutually exclusive):
  --all                Generate all characters
  --test               Generate test characters only
  --character NAME     Generate a specific character by name
  --archetype KEY      Generate all variants of an archetype

Options:
  --mode {portrait|background|composite|key_visual}   Generation mode (default: portrait)
  --seed INT           Fixed seed for reproducibility
  --output PATH        Output directory (default: <project>/generated-avatars)
  --dry-run            Validate prompts without API calls
  --post-process-only  Run circle-crop + compositing on existing images
```

## JSON Character Definition Format

See `characters/schema.json` for the full JSON Schema. Key structure:

```json
{
  "version": "1.0",
  "project": "my-project",
  "style": {
    "portrait_prompt": "Base style prompt...",
    "background_prompt": "Base background prompt...",
    "portrait_negative": "Things to avoid...",
    "background_negative": "Things to avoid in backgrounds...",
    "generation_params": {
      "model_id": "de7d3faf-762f-48e0-b3b7-9d0ac3a3fcf3",
      "width": 1024,
      "height": 1024,
      "guidance_scale": 7,
      "num_inference_steps": 30
    },
    "prompt_max_length": 1500
  },
  "characters": [
    {
      "name": "CharacterName",
      "character_prompt": "Specific character description..."
    }
  ]
}
```

### Optional Character Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `archetype` | string | Archetype key (groups characters) |
| `age_group` | string | `child`, `teen`, or `adult` |
| `gender` | string | For filename construction |
| `eye_color` | string | Explicit eye colour in prompt |
| `has_glasses` | boolean | Triggers glasses negative prompt |
| `bg_colours` | [string, string] | Background gradient colours |
| `bg_symbols` | string | Background symbol motifs |
| `background_prompt_override` | string | Replaces style background prompt entirely |
| `kv_prompt` | string | Key visual scene description (for `key_visual` mode) |
| `color_theme` | object | Colour theme (primary, secondary, accent) |

